menu "Rotation target backend"

config RT_WIFI_SSID
    string "WiFi SSID"
    default "changeme"
    help
        The network the device joins at boot. Credentials live in sdkconfig,
        which is gitignored - the MicroPython backend kept them out of git the
        same way, in wifi_credentials.py.

config RT_WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "WiFi password"
    default ""

config RT_WIFI_MAX_RETRIES
    int "WiFi connection attempts before giving up"
    default 10
    help
        The device keeps serving on its own once joined; this only bounds the
        initial connect. A range device that cannot reach the AP is useless, so
        exhausting the retries reboots rather than sitting idle.

config RT_DEV_ORIGIN
    string "Additional allowed CORS origin"
    default ""
    help
        An extra origin the webapp may be served from, e.g.
        "http://localhost:5173" while developing the frontend. Empty in a
        normal build - the device's own mDNS name and IP are always allowed.

config RT_SETUP_AP_PASSWORD
    string "Setup access-point password"
    default "rotationtarget"
    help
        Used only by the setup portal the device falls back to when it cannot
        join a network. WPA2 needs at least 8 characters; shorter than that and
        the AP comes up OPEN, which is logged loudly at boot.

config RT_HOSTNAME
    string "Hostname advertised over DHCP and mDNS"
    default "rotation-target"

endmenu
